Cell["\<\
Note: Facet contact occurs on branch 1 at \[Theta] = 0 and \[Pi] - (2\[Pi])/n \
     where n is the number of folds.\[LineSeparator]            Facet contact \
occurs on branch 2 at \[Theta] = (2\[Pi])/n and \[Pi]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816437992896964*^9, 
  3.816438099553019*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74cb390c-ca6c-4d7f-b7ed-\
336924a7b117"],

Cell["\<\
Note: a full cyclic permutation of the solution indices gives the same \
folding, just rigidly rotated. While technically you have 2^N choices for \
solution indices, many of them are the same in the sense that they are simply \
related through a rigid rotation (i.e. cyclic permutations of each other).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816436295185067*^9, 3.81643630629526*^9}, {
  3.816436346617928*^9, 3.816436359666666*^9}, {3.816436520981765*^9, 
  3.816436532531591*^9}, {3.8164366685914793`*^9, 
  3.81643684622789*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c85407cc-eb4b-48a4-a3d5-\
3a036bde4ff2"],

Cell["\<\
Note: reflecting \[Theta] about \[Pi]/2 (i.e. \[Theta] -> \[Pi] - \[Theta]) \
and changing the switch on all the solution indexes also gives the same \
structure (but reflected about the plane of the flat state)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816439772558906*^9, 3.816439827259124*^9}, {
  3.816439987367503*^9, 
  3.8164400075884447`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6bdadb07-57aa-42a1-926d-\
fd50243aa2ab"],

